# dev-meme-notifier — settings
#
# Edit the values below, save, and restart your agent (hooks load at session start).
# Anything you export as a real environment variable wins over what's here.

# Wait this many seconds after the agent asks for you before sounding the alarm.
WAKEUP_DELAY_SECS="${WAKEUP_DELAY_SECS:-10}"

# ...and only sound it if you haven't touched the keyboard or mouse for this long.
# Bump this to 45 if you want it to stay quiet unless you're really gone.
WAKEUP_IDLE_SECS="${WAKEUP_IDLE_SECS:-10}"

# Which moments arm the alarm. Delete any you don't want woken up for.
#   permission_prompt  - Agent is blocked waiting for you to approve a tool
#   idle_prompt        - Agent's own "still there?" nudge
#   agent_needs_input  - Agent is asking you a question mid-task
#   agent_completed    - a background agent finished
#   stop               - Agent finished responding
WAKEUP_EVENTS="${WAKEUP_EVENTS:-permission_prompt idle_prompt agent_needs_input agent_completed stop}"

# Video to play. Empty = pick a random .mp4/.mov/.webm/.gif from media/.
# If media/ is empty and WAKEUP_MEME_API is set, fetches from the API instead.
WAKEUP_VIDEO="${WAKEUP_VIDEO:-}"

# Video player. Options:
#   auto       - pick the best available (mpv > ffplay > vlc > quicktime on macOS)
#   mpv        - cross-platform, recommended (brew install mpv / apt install mpv)
#   ffplay     - comes with ffmpeg (brew install ffmpeg / apt install ffmpeg)
#   vlc        - VLC media player (must be in PATH)
#   quicktime  - macOS only, no install needed
WAKEUP_PLAYER="${WAKEUP_PLAYER:-auto}"

# Force system output volume to this (0-100) while the alarm plays, then put it back.
# Empty = leave your volume exactly as you left it.
# Works on macOS (osascript) and Linux (pactl/amixer).
WAKEUP_VOLUME="${WAKEUP_VOLUME:-}"

# 1 = keep replaying the video until you come back.
WAKEUP_LOOP="${WAKEUP_LOOP:-0}"

# Never play longer than this, no matter what.
WAKEUP_MAX_SECS="${WAKEUP_MAX_SECS:-120}"

# Idle seconds below this means you're back at the desk, so the alarm cuts out.
WAKEUP_RETURN_SECS="${WAKEUP_RETURN_SECS:-2}"

# Where decisions get logged.
WAKEUP_LOG="${WAKEUP_LOG:-$HOME/.claude/wakeup.log}"

# --- Meme API (optional) ---
# Fetch random dev memes when media/ has no files. Leave empty to disable.
# Supported sources:
#   reddit    - pulls from r/ProgrammerHumor (no API key needed, rate-limited)
#   imgflip   - imgflip.com popular memes (no API key needed)
#   giphy     - giphy.com trending/random GIFs (API key needed)
#   tenor     - tenor.com trending GIFs (API key needed)
#   custom    - your own URL (must return image/video URL or raw media)
# Examples:
#   WAKEUP_MEME_API="reddit"
#   WAKEUP_MEME_API="giphy"
#   WAKEUP_MEME_API="custom|https://your-api.com/random-meme"
WAKEUP_MEME_API="${WAKEUP_MEME_API:-}"

# Directory to store fetched memes and user-uploaded media.
# Defaults to media/ inside the project.
# WAKEUP_MEME_DIR defaults to media/ in common.sh — only set if you want a custom path
# WAKEUP_MEME_DIR=""

# --- API Keys (optional, only needed for key-required sources) ---
# Giphy API key — get free at https://developers.giphy.com/dashboard/
WAKEUP_GIPHY_API_KEY="${WAKEUP_GIPHY_API_KEY:-}"

# Tenor API key — get free at https://developers.google.com/tenor/guides/quickstart
WAKEUP_TENOR_API_KEY="${WAKEUP_TENOR_API_KEY:-}"

# Imgflip credentials (optional, lifts anonymous rate limits)
# Get at https://imgflip.com/signup
WAKEUP_IMGFLIP_USERNAME="${WAKEUP_IMGFLIP_USERNAME:-}"
WAKEUP_IMGFLIP_PASSWORD="${WAKEUP_IMGFLIP_PASSWORD:-}"

# Reddit OAuth (optional, lifts anonymous rate limits from 10 to 100 req/min)
# Create app at https://www.reddit.com/prefs/apps/ → select 'script' type
WAKEUP_REDDIT_CLIENT_ID="${WAKEUP_REDDIT_CLIENT_ID:-}"
WAKEUP_REDDIT_CLIENT_SECRET="${WAKEUP_REDDIT_CLIENT_SECRET:-}"
WAKEUP_REDDIT_USERNAME="${WAKEUP_REDDIT_USERNAME:-}"
WAKEUP_REDDIT_PASSWORD="${WAKEUP_REDDIT_PASSWORD:-}"

# Custom API headers (optional, only for 'custom' source)
# Format: "Header1: value1|Header2: value2" (pipe-separated)
WAKEUP_CUSTOM_HEADERS="${WAKEUP_CUSTOM_HEADERS:-}"

# How many API videos to keep cached (pre-fetched in background for zero latency)
# Default 5. Higher = more variety, more disk use.
WAKEUP_MEME_CACHE_SIZE="${WAKEUP_MEME_CACHE_SIZE:-5}"
